mod:for_pick_binding_source;
// WHAT A `for` OR `pick` BINDING HOLDS IS WHAT ITS SOURCE REACHES (DEF-517, HIGH by kind, landing 177d2b). A binding with no initialiser
// takes its value from its iterable or selector, and a read of one carried nothing of it, so a view of the caller's storage went back up through
// `for (int32[]:q in ps) { pass q; }` with no chain: the caller read freed bytes (each `v_*` here read 83/83 on main, no `=>!`, no lock). The same for
// a variadic slot: `pass vs[0i64]`, the slot being on the summary and its read on nothing. `b_*` is a pointer, `g_*` a guard over a pointer receiver
// (124/124 on main, a hang on a freed lock). `*_k` is each form's control, with no binding, refused on main. `x*` is a borrow of this frame's own local,
// BORROW-009 at the loop or the `pick`. `t*` is a selector's view of a temporary: one report at the selector, read or not. `y3` and `y4` are a refusal
// after a binding's read: its walk reports nothing and hands the reporting back. The right twins are `for_pick_binding_source_ok.npk`.
